# 🛰️ Earth Observation: Delhi Airshed — Complete Project Guide

> **SRIP 2026 | AI for Sustainability | IIT Gandhinagar**
> Prof. Nipun Batra's Lab

---

## 🎯 What Is This Project About?

**The Big Picture:** The Ministry of Environment wants to know **what the land around Delhi looks like from space** — where are the buildings? Where are the farms? Where is water? Where are the trees? This helps identify **pollution sources** (factories in built-up areas, crop burning in farmland, etc.).

**Your Job:** Build an AI pipeline that:
1. Takes **satellite photos** of the Delhi region
2. Figures out what **type of land** each photo shows (city? farm? forest? water?)
3. Trains a **CNN model** to automatically classify new satellite images

Think of it like building a **Google Maps + AI** for environmental auditing.

---

## 📦 The 4 Datasets — What Each Contains

### Dataset 1: Delhi-NCR Region Shapefile
- **Link:** [delhi_ncr_region.geojson](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rishabhsnip/earth-observation-delhi-airshed?select=delhi_ncr_region.geojson)
- **What it is:** A GeoJSON file containing the **geographic boundary** of the Delhi National Capital Region
- **Think of it as:** An outline/border drawn on a map — like tracing the edge of Delhi-NCR on Google Maps
- **CRS:** EPSG:4326 (latitude/longitude coordinates)
- **Size:** ~4.6 MB (detailed boundary with many points)
- **Why you need it:** To know **which area** we're working in and filter only relevant satellite images

### Dataset 2: Sentinel-2 RGB Image Patches
- **Link:** [rgb folder](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rishabhsnip/earth-observation-delhi-airshed?select=rgb)
- **What it is:** **9,216 satellite photos** taken by the ESA Sentinel-2 satellite
- **Each image:** 128×128 pixels, RGB (3 color channels), [.png](file:///C:/Users/kush3/.gemini/antigravity/brain/cef416aa-c801-488e-8cd1-849bcb6d317a/eo_helping_fig1.png) format
- **Resolution:** 10 meters per pixel → each image covers **1.28 km × 1.28 km** of ground
- **Filename format:** `latitude_longitude.png` (e.g., `28.2056_76.8558.png`)
  - This tells you the **center coordinate** of what the image shows
- **Think of it as:** 9,216 tiny square photos of different parts of Delhi-NCR taken from space, laid out in a grid

### Dataset 3: Delhi Airshed Shapefile
- **Link:** [delhi_airshed.geojson](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rishabhsnip/earth-observation-delhi-airshed?select=delhi_airshed.geojson)
- **What it is:** Boundary of the **Delhi Airshed** — the atmospheric region where pollution from Delhi spreads
- **Size:** ~5.8 KB (simpler boundary than NCR)
- **Think of it as:** A smaller, specific zone within the larger NCR region. The airshed is the area where Delhi's air quality is affected
- **Why you need it:** Context for the environmental audit (but the main filtering uses the NCR boundary)

### Dataset 4: ESA WorldCover 2021 (land_cover.tif)
- **Link:** [worldcover_bbox_delhi_ncr_2021.tif](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rishabhsnip/earth-observation-delhi-airshed?select=worldcover_bbox_delhi_ncr_2021.tif)
- **What it is:** A **raster image** where each pixel is labeled with what type of land it represents
- **Size:** 92 MB, 9600×9602 pixels
- **Resolution:** 10m/pixel (same as Sentinel-2 images)
- **Source:** ESA WorldCover 2021 — a global land cover map created by the European Space Agency
- **Each pixel value is a class code:**

| Code | Land Cover Type | % of Delhi-NCR Area |
|:---:|:---|:---:|
| 10 | 🌳 Tree cover | 10.4% |
| 20 | 🌿 Shrubland | 3.3% |
| 30 | 🌾 Grassland | 7.1% |
| 40 | 🌾 Cropland | **53.5%** ← Most common |
| 50 | 🏙️ Built-up | **23.3%** ← Second |
| 60 | 🏜️ Bare/sparse vegetation | 1.7% |
| 80 | 💧 Permanent water | 0.7% |
| 90 | 🌊 Herbaceous wetland | ~0% |

- **Think of it as:** A "color-by-number" map where each pixel is colored by land type. You use this as the **answer key** — it tells you what label each satellite image should get.

